Problem Statement 1: Kth Smallest Element in BST
Write a C++ program to create a Binary Search Tree (BST) using the given elements.
Find the kth smallest element without separately sorting the input elements.
Use inorder traversal (Left, Root, Right) to access elements in ascending order.
Validate the value of k based on the total number of nodes in the BST.
Display the kth smallest element or an appropriate error message if k is invalid.
